{
  "info": {
    "name": "SlotFlow API v1",
    "description": "Appointment booking for small service businesses.\n\n## Before you start\n\n1. Set `base_url` (defaults to `http://localhost:8000`).\n2. Run **Auth \u2192 Log in**. It stores the bearer token in `token` automatically, so every other request just works.\n3. Run **Availability \u2192 Find slots** and paste a `starts_at` into **Bookings \u2192 Create a booking**.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- **Workspace**: every request needs one. Send `X-Tenant: <slug>`, or authenticate \u2014 a token carries its own and takes precedence.\n- **Time**: UTC on the wire, ISO-8601 with an offset. Anything that renders a time for a human takes a required `tz` (an IANA name such as `Europe/Vienna`). Offsets and abbreviations are rejected \u2014 neither can express daylight saving.\n- **Money**: integer minor units plus a currency code.\n- **Errors**: one shape, always \u2014 `{ \"error\": { \"code\", \"message\", \u2026 } }`. Branch on `error.code`.\n\n## The one worth reading\n\n`POST /bookings` returns **409 `slot_unavailable`** when the slot went between the customer seeing it and confirming it. On a busy diary that is a normal Tuesday, not a failure: refresh availability and offer another time.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000",
      "description": "Where the app is running."
    },
    {
      "key": "tenant",
      "value": "bright-lane",
      "description": "Workspace slug of the seeded demo studio."
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Filled in by 'Log in'."
    },
    {
      "key": "tz",
      "value": "Europe/Vienna",
      "description": "Your IANA timezone. Slots come back rendered in it."
    },
    {
      "key": "service_id",
      "value": "1"
    },
    {
      "key": "staff_id",
      "value": "1"
    },
    {
      "key": "booking_reference",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Filled in by 'Create a booking'."
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "description": "Token authentication. Send the token as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register a customer",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant",
                "value": "{{tenant}}",
                "description": "The workspace. Ignored when a token is sent \u2014 a token carries its own."
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/register",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Creates a customer account in the workspace named by `X-Tenant`, and returns a token.\n\nIf the address already has guest bookings, they are adopted \u2014 so the customer keeps their history, and therefore their risk profile.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Ada Lovelace\",\n  \"email\": \"ada@example.test\",\n  \"password\": \"correct-horse-battery\",\n  \"password_confirmation\": \"correct-horse-battery\",\n  \"phone\": \"+43 660 1234567\",\n  \"timezone\": \"Europe/Vienna\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('token', pm.response.json().data.token);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Log in",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant",
                "value": "{{tenant}}",
                "description": "The workspace. Ignored when a token is sent \u2014 a token carries its own."
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Exchanges credentials for a bearer token, and stores it in the `token` variable.\n\nSeeded demo accounts (password `password` for all three):\n- `owner@slotflow.test` \u2014 full admin\n- `maya@slotflow.test` \u2014 staff, sees only her own diary\n- `customer@slotflow.test` \u2014 customer",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"owner@slotflow.test\",\n  \"password\": \"password\",\n  \"device_name\": \"Postman\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('token', pm.response.json().data.token);",
                  "    console.log('Token stored.');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Who am I",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant",
                "value": "{{tenant}}",
                "description": "The workspace. Ignored when a token is sent \u2014 a token carries its own."
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/me",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The authenticated user and their workspace."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Log out",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant",
                "value": "{{tenant}}",
                "description": "The workspace. Ignored when a token is sent \u2014 a token carries its own."
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/logout",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "logout"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Revokes only the token used for this request. Other devices stay signed in."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
